# out_rev = 1 (the phases in the other order, as id_pmsm finds them): the F4
# flipped the q current and the angle for the F3, but not the speed. The F3
# advances the angle by that speed between packets and uses it in its
# current predictor for the back-EMF (curpid.c): unflipped, the current fell
# short in proportion to the speed (2 vel psi / l dt). At 150 mm/s on the
# bench motor: 0.133 A measured for 0.229 A commanded (the pid wound up);
# now 0.141 for 0.130 (DEBUGNOTES 2026-11-16).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
hv0.sim_phase_rev = 1
conf0.out_rev = 1
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 3
lcnc 1 150
run 2
pmsm_ttc0.cur
hv0.iq_fb
vel1.vel
fault0.fault
@expect hv0.iq_fb ~ =pmsm_ttc0.cur 15%
@expect fault0.fault == 0
